      <activity id="097f2086-ca9d-5c1d-9a80-69daa2965480" activityNameId="9eb76557-289c-564f-9429-ce7cacfbc38b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Industrial residue wood, softwood, forest-debarked, u=70%, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Industrial residue wood, softwood, forest-debarked, u=70%, at plant
The volume refers to the wood not including the bark. The multi-output process "sawing, softwood, forest-debarked, at plant" delivers the two coproducts "sawn timber, softwood, raw, forest-debarked, u=70%, at plant" and "industrial residue wood, softwood, forest-debarked, u=70%, at plant". Allocation is based on the over-all proceeds of the process.;
UUID: b4f43da2-8193-3b89-8383-f6a0de1f403e
Includes transports of debarked roundwood from forest, sawing a sawmill
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Technology mix used in Germany 1986
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: The assumption that Germany is representative for central Europe is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b4f43da2-8193-3b89-8383-f6a0de1f403e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
